From bc0c698c1b55f3ceb3ec4d2d573a81d100f52fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:50:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Decide single-player natively for the developer mutation gate

The mutation gate (Lua.Eval, convar writes and console commands, memory,
detours, Remix options outside rtx.*) called the client realm's
game.SinglePlayer. A remote server's client scripts can replace that
function and the server replicates sv_cheats, so a player who launched with
-insecure passed the gate on a malicious insecure server.

Single-player now comes from the engine client: connected, a loopback net
channel (IVEngineClient::GetNetChannelInfo()->IsLoopback(), address type
NA_LOOPBACK, which only the server running in this process has), no demo
playback and one player slot. -insecure still comes from the process command
line and sv_cheats from the cvar system. The rendering gate's client-realm
check compares the module's state with lua_shared's client state instead of
reading the CLIENT_DLL/SERVER/MENU_DLL globals.

The pure decision is in source/session_policy.h, tested by
tests/session_policy_test.cpp. The vtable slots it uses (CEngineClient 21,
27, 72 and 76; CNetChan 6) were checked against GMod x64 engine.dll through
RTTI. Version 0.2.1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
